The task is short and local: mine to the hold limit, then sell everything in the hold. Since I'm already at `sol_belt`, I loop `mine()` and break on `HoldFull`; any other failure has no plan, so I re-fail the program with it. Then I `goTo('sol_base')` (docks) and `sell` every row in the hold, naming each.

```ts
import {Effect, Either} from 'effect';
import {goTo, mine, sell, note, orient} from 'play';

export default Effect.gen(function* () {
  // Mine at the belt I'm at until the hold is full.
  for (;;) {
    const step = yield* mine().pipe(Effect.either);
    if (Either.isLeft(step)) {
      if (step.left._tag === 'HoldFull') {
        yield* note('hold full, heading to base');
        break;
      }
      // Not a planned failure: re-fail the program with it.
      return yield* Effect.fail(step.left);
    }
  }

  // Fly home (docks) and sell everything in the hold, naming every row.
  yield* goTo('sol_base');
  const here = yield* orient();
  const sold = yield* sell(here.cargo.map(r => ({item_id: r.item_id})));
  yield* note(`sold for ${sold.total}`);
});
```

